{"type": "mitigation_summary", "mitigation_summary": {"action": "Add a second, faster-tripping rate-based rule (`rate-limit-fast`, 100 req/60s per IP, Block) to WebACL `shield-sample-webacl` as a defense-in-depth backstop — leaving the proven `rate-limit` rule unchanged.", "reasoning": "The flood was stopped solely by the rate-based `rate-limit` rule (100/300s per IP); the Anti-DDoS AMR never declared an event and gave zero mitigation, and the single rule leaked ~34k requests during its ~14–15s per-IP detection delay. A parallel 60s-window rule trips faster (shrinking the leak) and removes the single-rule dependency. Forward-looking hardening — the incident self-recovered, so there is no emergency rollback and no active outage."}, "execution_plan": [{"number": "1", "step": "prepare", "instructions": [{"number": "1.1", "instruction": {"type": "command", "content": "aws wafv2 get-web-acl --name shield-sample-webacl --scope CLOUDFRONT --id f7e012b0-0915-4efd-84cf-f04428eafb38 --region us-east-1 > webacl-backup.json"}, "reasoning": {"purpose": "Capture the current 12-rule configuration and live LockToken as the authoritative rollback baseline before any change.", "risks": [], "advisory": []}}]}, {"number": "2", "step": "pre_validate", "instructions": [{"number": "2.1", "instruction": {"type": "command", "content": "aws wafv2 get-web-acl --name shield-sample-webacl --scope CLOUDFRONT --id f7e012b0-0915-4efd-84cf-f04428eafb38 --region us-east-1 --query 'WebACL.Rules[].Name'"}, "reasoning": {"purpose": "Verify the live WebACL still holds the expected 12 rules and the LockToken is unchanged, so the update applies against the expected state.", "risks": [], "advisory": []}}]}, {"number": "3", "step": "apply", "instructions": [{"number": "3.1", "instruction": {"type": "command", "content": "aws wafv2 update-web-acl --name shield-sample-webacl --scope CLOUDFRONT --id f7e012b0-0915-4efd-84cf-f04428eafb38 --default-action Allow={} --visibility-config SampledRequestsEnabled=true,CloudWatchMetricsEnabled=true,MetricName=shield-sample-webacl --lock-token <LOCKTOKEN_FROM_PREPARE> --rules file://webacl-rules-13.json --region us-east-1"}, "reasoning": {"purpose": "Append a faster-tripping rate-based backstop without modifying the existing proven `rate-limit` rule.", "risks": ["update-web-acl REPLACES the entire rule list — the file must contain all 12 existing rules byte-for-byte plus the new rule (13 total); omitting any silently deletes that protection.", "100/60s per-IP is more aggressive than 100/300s and could block a legitimate client sustaining >100 req/min from one IP — watch for false positives in post_validate."], "advisory": []}}, {"number": "3.2", "instruction": {"type": "command", "content": "{
