}"}, "reasoning": {"purpose": "The new rule to append at priority 12, alongside the 12 existing rules.", "risks": [], "advisory": []}}]}, {"number": "4", "step": "post_validate", "instructions": [{"number": "4.1", "instruction": {"type": "command", "content": "aws wafv2 get-web-acl --name shield-sample-webacl --scope CLOUDFRONT --id f7e012b0-0915-4efd-84cf-f04428eafb38 --region us-east-1 --query 'WebACL.Rules[].{Name:Name,Priority:Priority}'"}, "reasoning": {"purpose": "Confirm the WebACL now has 13 rules including `rate-limit-fast` at priority 12 and the original `rate-limit` at priority 6 is intact.", "risks": [], "advisory": []}}, {"number": "4.2", "instruction": {"type": "command", "content": "aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics --namespace AWS/CloudFront --metric-name Requests --dimensions Name=DistributionId,Value=E2SGKO2JTMC4PT --start-time <WINDOW_START> --end-time <WINDOW_END> --period 300 --statistics Sum --region us-east-1"}, "reasoning": {"purpose": "Confirm legitimate traffic to cf-httpecho.a.example.com stays near baseline (repeat for 4xxErrorRate, Average). Query CloudFront metrics in us-east-1 with NO Region dimension.", "risks": [], "advisory": []}}]}, {"number": "5", "step": "rollback", "instructions": [{"number": "5.1", "instruction": {"type": "command", "content": "aws wafv2 get-web-acl ... --query 'LockToken'  # re-fetch latest token
aws wafv2 update-web-acl --name shield-sample-webacl --scope CLOUDFRONT --id f7e012b0-0915-4efd-84cf-f04428eafb38 --default-action Allow={} --visibility-config SampledRequestsEnabled=true,CloudWatchMetricsEnabled=true,MetricName=shield-sample-webacl --lock-token <LATEST_LOCKTOKEN> --rules file://webacl-backup-rules.json --region us-east-1"}, "reasoning": {"purpose": "Restore the exact pre-change 12-rule config if the new rule causes false positives. The proven `rate-limit` rule stays in effect throughout, so rollback carries no DDoS-exposure risk.", "risks": [], "advisory": []}}]}], "code_change_spec": {"requirements": [{"objective": "Codify a faster-tripping rate-based backstop and strengthen the L7 DDoS posture of `shield-sample-webacl` in IaC.", "description": "Add the `rate-limit-fast` rule (100/60s per IP, Block) to the WebACL definition alongside the existing `rate-limit` rule, and evaluate tightening the primary threshold and/or the Anti-DDoS managed group so the posture no longer depends on resource-level event detection that failed to engage for a short, concentrated flood. Keep both rate-based rules independently defined so neither is a sole point of defense.", "acceptance_criteria": ["The IaC-managed `shield-sample-webacl` includes both `rate-limit` (100/300s) and `rate-limit-fast` (100/60s), each AggregateKeyType IP, Action Block.", "A deploy reconciles live WebACL state to this definition (manual rule drift reverted on deploy).", "A post-deploy validation confirms legitimate CloudFront traffic to cf-httpecho.a.example.com is unaffected (request volume and 4xx rate at baseline, measured with no Region dimension)."]}]}}

{"id": "e3fba5d5-cc4d-4c95-a064-ff875b042bbc", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Now confirmed precisely. Every BLOCK record carries exactly one label `awswaf:managed:aws:anti-ddos:challengeable-request` (no `event-detected`, no `ddos-request`, no suspicion labels). The ALLOW records in the window carry `awswaf:managed:token:absent`.

Key interpretation: The Anti-DDoS AMR added the `challengeable-request` label (it classified these as challengeable), but it did NOT declare an event (`event-detected` absent) and did NOT itself terminate the requests. The terminating rule was `rate-limit` (the rate-based rule, limitKey IP), action BLOCK. The AMR's own sub-rules (ChallengeAllDuringEvent / ChallengeDDoSRequests / DDoSRequests) did NOT fire — no CHALLENGE/CAPTCHA at all.

Now the rate-based delay analysis. Each top IP shows 0 ALLOW in the window — meaning they were blocked immediately. Let me verify the per-IP first-ALLOW vs first-BLOCK timing to confirm there was essentially no detection delay (or quantify it) for a couple of IPs across the full ramp (04:15 onward).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_lbgyzUC7UUuKZkT7HlztZy", "tool_name": "query_cloudwatch_logs", "input": {"aws_account_id": "012345678901_1", "aws_region": "us-east-1", "end_time": 1788841320, "log_group": "aws-waf-logs-group", "query": "filter webaclId like '/webacl/shield-sample-webacl/' and (httpRequest.clientIp='65.2.111.194' or httpRequest.clientIp='13.207.5.101' or httpRequest.clientIp='3.238.251.86') | stats earliest(@timestamp) as first_req, latest(@timestamp) as last_req, count() as total, sum(action='ALLOW') as allow, sum(action='BLOCK') as block by httpRequest.clientIp as ip | sort total desc | limit 5", "start_time": 1788841140}, "type": "tool_use"}, {"id": "tooluse_WyM38rCXoXPGTZddbTEPgN", "tool_name": "query_cloudwatch_logs", "input": {"aws_account_id": "012345678901_1", "aws_region": "us-east-1", "end_time": 1788841320, "log_group": "aws-waf-logs-group", "query": "filter webaclId like '/webacl/shield-sample-webacl/' and httpRequest.clientIp='65.2.111.194' | stats earliest(@timestamp) as first_any, count() as c by action | sort action asc | limit 5", "start_time": 1788840900}, "type": "tool_use"}], "user_reference": null}
